Character class with enough ranges to grow the regexp class allocation
(regexp.c reallocs the class in DCLASS-sized steps once it overflows the
initial buffer). The substitution replaces every letter a-i with X.
args: -d input

-- stdin --
,s/[a-cd-fg-i]/X/g
,p
q
-- stdout --
XXXXXXXXXj
-- stderr --
 -. input
?changed files
-- input --
abcdefghij
